<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:16:Real Mode">
<!--
    kuna #1288: an x86 real-mode near branch wraps IP inside its code segment,
    and a real-mode address is the linear CS*16 + IP, where CS need not be a
    multiple of 0x1000. kuna's GH-7418 fix (tests/stages/
    gh7418-x86-call-rel16-mask.xml) masked every rel16 target to its low 16
    bits, which is right only for CS 0, so a DOS program loaded at segment
    0x1000 lost all but 12 of its 330 functions. The linear sum is right only
    when IP does not wrap.

    16-bit x86 decodes with x86-16.sla, which keeps CS in the context variable
    realCS (default 0). A far CALL states its target's CS; 0x2b58 is the main
    code segment of that program:

        00100  e8 00 90        CALL 0x9103   ; CS 0, IP 0x0103 - 0x7000 wraps
        40000  9a f8 00 58 2b  CALLF 2b58:00f8 (0x2b678)
        40005  9a f8 00 58 4b  CALLF 4b58:00f8 (0x4b678)
        4000a  9a 80 01 58 2b  CALLF 2b58:0180 (0x2b700)
        4000f  9a a0 01 58 2b  CALLF 2b58:01a0 (0x2b720)
        40014  9a fd ff 58 2b  CALLF 2b58:fffd (0x3b57d)
        2b678  e8 ae 93        CALL 0x34a29  ; CS 0x2b58, IP 0x00fb - 0x6c52 wraps
        4b678  e8 ae 93        CALL 0x54a29  ; CS 0x4b58, the same wrap
        5b680  e8 8d 49        CALL 0x60010  ; CS 0 cannot hold 0x5b680: linear sum
        2b700  2e a1 10 00     MOV AX,CS:[0x10]  ; reads 2b58:0010, linear 0x2b590
        2b720  9a 00 00 00 70  CALLF 7000:0000 (0x70000) ; pushes IP 0x01a5
        3b57d  e8 a3 00        CALL 0x2b623  ; ends on the segment's last byte: IP 0x0000 + 0xa3

    Stage: P1/P2 decode (x86 SLEIGH spec fix, no option). Without realCS the
    mask decodes 0x4a29 for both wrapped calls, the linear sum 0x24a29 and
    0x44a29, and the linear sum also decodes the first call to -0x6efd. A near
    CALL pushes IP inside its segment (0x00fb), not the low half of its linear
    address (0xb67b), and a CS: override reads CS 0x2b58, not the 64 KiB block
    guess 0x2000. A far CALL pushes IP in its own segment (0x01a5), not the low
    half of its linear address (0xb725), and an instruction that ends on its
    segment's last byte wraps IP to 0 (0x2b623, not 0x3b623).

    The script pins option segmentize off: asserts #7 and #11 read each
    pushed IP as a store through segment(), which the default folds into the
    stack frame (see kuna-segmentize.xml).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100">
e80090c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x9103">
b80700c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x2b678">
